From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: airoha: npu: add DMA pool memory region

The EN7581 NPU can only address host DRAM at 0x80000000-0xbfffffff;
higher addresses alias the lower 1 GiB. Allow an optional shared DMA
pool so coherent buffers shared with the NPU can be kept inside that
window.

7.3 and 7.4 already describe the WLAN Block Ack region and the
firmware-name property, so only the extra region is added here.
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/airoha,en7581-npu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/airoha,en7581-npu.yaml
@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@
       - description: NPU wlan offload TX buffers region
       - description: NPU wlan offload TX packet identifiers region
       - description: NPU wlan Block Ack buffers region
+      - description: Coherent DMA pool for buffers shared with the NPU
     minItems: 1
 
   memory-region-names:
@@ -57,6 +58,7 @@
       - const: tx-pkt
       - const: tx-bufid
       - const: ba
+      - const: dma
     minItems: 1
 
   firmware-name:
